## Accessibility

- All interactive elements must be keyboard navigable
- Focus indicators must be visible (never `outline: none` without a replacement)
- Color contrast must meet WCAG 2.1 AA (4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for large text)
- Images and icons used as actions must have `aria-label` or `alt` text
- Form inputs must have associated `<label>` elements

---

## Working conventions

- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` unless content is sanitized server-side; document the reason inline
- TypeScript interfaces that mirror backend serializer fields must be updated in the same commit when a field is added or removed
- Never remove a field from a shared interface without confirming it is unreferenced across the entire frontend
- After changing component behavior (placeholder text, button labels, API surface), run the affected test file locally before committing
- Grep for changed string literals across test files when renaming UI copy: `grep -r 'old text' [test dir]/`
